---
description: Rules for writing documentation under docs/ - claim tags, ADR format, facts versus assumptions, English.
globs: docs/**/*.md
alwaysApply: false
---

- Write in English, without exceptions.
- Tag every factual claim: `Verified (YYYY-MM-DD, source)` with a URL, command or commit as the source, `Assumed`, or
  `Unverified`. Keep facts and assumptions visibly separate. An untested OS is never "verified".
- Cite sources as full URLs with the date you read them.
- No `TODO` or `TBD` outside a section named "Open questions".
- ADRs live in `docs/adr/NNNN-title.md`. Sections: Status (Proposed, Accepted, Superseded by NNNN), Context, Options (a
  table with pros, cons and the evidence tag for each), Decision, Consequences, Facts versus assumptions, Revisit
  triggers.
- Specs state exact values and limits (formats, sizes, field names) so another agent can implement them without
  guessing.
- No machine-specific paths, usernames or secrets; the repository is public.
- Use relative links between documents and keep the Markdown lint-clean.
